## Trust Boundaries

```
UNTRUSTED
    ↓ (public internet)
EDGE ROUTER                     ← Trust boundary 1
    ↓ (NAT #1 — home subnet)
MIDDLE ROUTER                   ← Trust boundary 2
    ↓ (NAT #2 — middle subnet)
SCRYPTGATE                      ← Hardware trust anchor
SERVER                          ← Trust boundary 3
    ↓ (NAT #3 / routing)
LABS NETWORK                    ← Highest trust zone
    ↓
QUBES VAULT-QUBE                ← Absolute trust anchor
                                   (no network interface — ever)
```

Nothing crosses a trust boundary without explicit permission. ScryptGate sits at boundary 3 as a hardware oracle — its results are treated as more trusted than any software component at the same layer.

