## Threat Actors

### T1 — Remote Attacker (Internet)

```
Capabilities:
    → Network access to public IP only
    → Can probe port 443 and WireGuard UDP port
    → Cannot reach any internal subnet directly
    → May attempt to exploit public-facing services

Motivation: opportunistic, targeted, or automated scanning
```

### T2 — Local Network Attacker (Home Network)

```
Capabilities:
    → Access to home subnet (YOUR_HOME_SUBNET)
    → Cannot reach middle subnet or labs
    → Can attempt to reach edge router admin interface
    → May be a compromised home device

Motivation: lateral movement, credential theft
```

### T3 — Compromised Middle Router

```
Capabilities:
    → Full control of middle subnet
    → Can intercept traffic between edge and server
    → Can send malicious proposals to approval API
    → Cannot reach labs directly

Motivation: pivot to server, inject malicious agent actions
```

### T4 — Compromised Server Process

```
Capabilities:
    → Control of one or more Podman containers
    → Can attempt to escape to host via SELinux bypass
    → Can attempt to reach labs network
    → Can attempt to call ScryptGate API maliciously

Motivation: persistence, data exfiltration, lateral movement
```

### T5 — Physical Attacker

```
Capabilities:
    → Physical access to any device
    → Can attempt cold boot attacks on RAM
    → Can attempt to read LUKS-encrypted drives
    → Can steal ScryptGate ASIC

Motivation: data theft, infrastructure takeover
```

