## Attack Surface

### External Attack Surface (Internet-Facing)

```
Port 443/TCP     → Caddy TLS → frontend/backend only
                   Rate limited, security headers, TLS 1.3 only
                   Backend not directly reachable

WireGuard UDP    → Key-authenticated only
                   No response to unauthenticated packets
                   Effectively invisible to scanners
```

**Total external attack surface: two endpoints.**  
Everything else is filtered at the edge router.

### Internal Attack Surface (Per Trust Zone)

```
Home subnet:
    → Edge router admin (HTTPS + SSH, key auth only)
    → WireGuard server endpoint

Middle subnet:
    → Middle router LuCI (HTTPS, key auth, LAN only)
    → Server wlan0 (no services exposed, uplink only)
    → ScryptGate API (HTTP, local network only)

Labs subnet:
    → Server eth0 (gateway only, no admin services on this interface)
    → Qubes workstation (SSH, key auth)
    → Secondary device (SSH, key auth)

Server internal:
    → Caddy (443 only, proxies to containers)
    → Approval API (8443, mTLS, restricted IPs only)
    → Grafana (localhost:3000, WireGuard access only)
    → Prometheus (localhost:9090, internal only)
    → Chroma (container network only)
    → Inference worker (container network only, mTLS)
```

