## Fail-Safe Analysis

Every security component in this architecture is designed to fail **closed** — meaning failure results in more restriction, not less.

|Component                 |Failure Mode                   |Fail Behavior              |Acceptable? |
|--------------------------|-------------------------------|---------------------------|------------|
|ScryptGate unreachable    |Network issue, hardware failure|All proposals rejected     |✅ Yes — safe|
|ScryptGate returns invalid|Tampered hardware, bug         |Proposal rejected          |✅ Yes — safe|
|Approval API down         |Container crash                |No approvals possible      |✅ Yes — safe|
|Vault unreachable         |Qubes shutdown                 |Model load rejected        |✅ Yes — safe|
|wlan0 down                |Wi-Fi drop, router reboot      |Labs go dark               |✅ Yes — safe|
|WireGuard down            |Key mismatch, network          |Remote access lost         |✅ Yes — safe|
|Caddy TLS error           |Cert expired, ACME fail        |Site unreachable           |✅ Yes — safe|
|SELinux deny              |Container escape attempt       |Action blocked, logged     |✅ Yes — safe|
|LUKS not mounted          |Reboot without unlock          |Podman stack fails to start|✅ Yes — safe|

**No component in this architecture fails open.**

