## Security Assumptions

This threat model assumes:

```
A1. The edge router firmware is not backdoored at manufacture
A2. The middle router OpenWrt build is from official sources
A3. The ASIC hardware has not been physically tampered with
A4. The Qubes vault-qube never receives a network interface
A5. The admin Ed25519 private key never leaves the vault-qube
A6. The LUKS passphrase is not stored digitally anywhere
A7. Physical access to the premises is controlled
A8. The human reviewer does not approve obviously malicious proposals
A9. Podman and the Linux kernel have no actively exploited zero-days
A10. Scrypt, Ed25519, and AES-256 have no known practical breaks
```

If any assumption is violated the threat model may not hold. Assumptions A1-A3 and A7 require physical security measures outside the scope of this document.

