## Incident Response

### Suspected Compromise — Middle Router

```
1. Disconnect middle router WAN from edge router immediately
2. Labs go dark (kill switch activates automatically)
3. Access edge router from home network — review logs
4. Review MSI syslog for any proposals sent from middle router
5. Review ScryptGate logs for unusual verification patterns
6. Factory reset middle router — reflash OpenWrt from known good image
7. Rotate middle router SSH keys and watchdog agent HMAC key
8. Reconnect and monitor closely for 48 hours
```

### Suspected Compromise — Server Container

```
1. Identify which container via SELinux audit log
2. Stop compromised container: podman stop <container>
3. Do NOT delete — preserve for forensics
4. Review container logs for exfiltration attempts
5. Check if container attempted to reach labs subnet
6. Rebuild container from clean image
7. Review all other containers for lateral movement signs
8. Rotate any credentials the compromised container had access to
```

### WireGuard Key Suspected Stolen

```
1. Immediately: ASUS GUI → VPN → WireGuard → delete affected peer
2. Generate new keypair in vault-qube
3. Add new public key as peer on ASUS
4. Distribute new config to legitimate device
5. Review WireGuard handshake logs for unauthorized connections
6. If unauthorized connections found: audit what was accessed via VPN
```

### ScryptGate ASIC Stolen

```
1. Reference hashes in vault-qube become orphaned
2. All model loads will fail — system halts safely
3. No automated agent actions possible
4. Human-only operation until replacement ASIC is acquired
5. New ASIC: re-run model integrity baseline
6. Update vault-qube reference hashes with new ASIC's hash output
```

